      <scope classrefs="Rational" doc="This class implements rational numbers.&#10;In the two-argument form of the constructor, Fraction(8, 6) will produce a rational number equivalent to 4/3. Both arguments must be Rational. The numerator defaults to 0 and the denominator defaults to 1 so that Fraction(3) == 3 and Fraction() == 0.  Fractions can also be constructed from:  - numeric strings similar to those accepted by the float constructor (for example, '-2.3' or '1e10') " ilk="class" line="44" lineend="605" name="Fraction">
