    <scope doc="OS routines for Mac, NT, or Posix depending on what system we're on.&#10;This exports: - all functions from posix, nt, os2, or ce, e.g. unlink, stat, etc. - os.path is one of the modules posixpath, or ntpath - os.name is 'posix', 'nt', 'os2', 'ce' or 'riscos' - os.curdir is a string representing the current directory ('.' or ':') - os.pardir is a string representing the parent directory ('..' or '::') - os.sep is the (or a most common) pathname separator ('/' or ':' or '\\') - os.extsep is the extension separator ('.' or '/') - os.altsep is the alternate pathname separator (None or '/') - os.pathsep is the component separator used in $PATH etc" ilk="blob" lang="Python" name="os">
