      <scope classrefs="object" doc="imap(func, *iterables) --&gt; imap object&#10;Make an iterator that computes the function using arguments from each of the iterables.  Like map() except that it returns an iterator instead of a list and that it stops when the shortest iterable is exhausted instead of filling in None for shorter iterables." ilk="class" name="map">
        <scope doc="x.__iter__() &lt;==&gt; iter(x)" ilk="function" name="__iter__" signature="x.__iter__() &lt;==&gt; iter(x)" />
