      <scope classrefs="object" doc="property(fget=None, fset=None, fdel=None, doc=None) -&gt; property attribute&#10;fget is a function to be used for getting an attribute value, and likewise fset is a function for setting, and fdel a function for del'ing, an attribute.  Typical use is to define a managed attribute x: class C(object): def getx(self): return self._x def setx(self, value): self._x = value def delx(self): del self._x x = property(getx, setx, delx, &quot;I'm the 'x' property.&quot;)  Decorators make defining new properties or modifying existing ones easy:" ilk="class" name="property">
