      <scope classrefs="object" doc="xrange([start,] stop[, step]) -&gt; xrange object&#10;Like range(), but instead of returning a list, returns an object that generates the numbers in the range on demand.  For looping, this is slightly faster than range() and more memory efficient." ilk="class" name="XRangeType">
